div.p:
Two brigades of colored troops participated in the victory at Nashville, December 15, 1864.

The heaviest loss in any regiment on that field occurred in the Thirteenth U. S. Colored Infantry, which, in its assault on Overton Hill, lost 55 killed (including 4 officers), and 166 wounded;



Includes the mortally wounded. total, 221.

